ng them to the reserve near  chiang mai  the camp owners themselves contacted  shiloh's foundation  and asked for help as hardly any  tourists are coming to ride the  elephants  due to the coronavirus pandemic  an adult elephant is usually worth about  2 million baht  or more than 50 000 but due to the  pandemic  the animals have become more of a burden  for their owners  it costs them nearly a thousand euros a  month for food and care  thanapot kayer is happy to at least get  1 million baht per elephant from chile's  foundation  our situation has been dire since the  start of the pandemic  we had to close the camp for months  but regardless of whether we're open or  closed we still have to take care of the  elephants  and we need to feed them every day we  were allowed to reopen on july 1st  but there are simply no visitors  the camp owner and his elephant tamers  don't want us to look too closely as the  animals are loaded onto the trucks  they say that for safety reasons we must  keep our distance  elephants they are not really easy to go  on the truck  because when they put in the truck is  mean their life will be chained again  they experience with many times move  from one place to other places  and they might be abused from one place  to the others  so now they think they will take them  somewhere which is they're not quite  sure  before setting off the elephants must be  fixed into place on the platforms  each animal gets its own frame made of  bamboo stalks  the elephants and the rescuers have a  journey of about 800 kilometers ahead of  them  the team has never transported so many  animals at once over such a long  distance  the convoy sets off in the early  afternoon  after less than half an hour the  vehicles have to make a stop  one of the elephants went into a rampage  on the truck bed and destroyed the  restraining bars holding it in place  now they have a major repair job on  their hands  many of them are nervous this is all the  time when we transport  they will start to damage and they  broken  the frame and throw the frame to the  road  and if we if we keep carrying on they  will take over the truck  after about an hour the problem is fixed  and the adventure can continue  the elephants now seem somewhat more  relaxed  the rescuers knew just what to do to  calm them down  most important they love to eat so  as long as they feel here they're not  they  they're not hungry and no one hit them  no one  beaten them i think the journey okay  the rest of the journey does indeed go  smoothly  the cool dusk is refreshing for both the  elephants and their rescuers  the next morning after a nearly 20-hour  drive the convoy reaches its destination  the elephant nature park north of chiang  mai the team is exhausted  black chillard has hardly slept but  nothing can dampen her mood  all of them happy because the journey is  quite stressed  elephant angry so now they are right  home  i feel relieved  once the restraining bars have been  removed it's time for the elephants to  take their first cautious steps  into a new life  the newcomers will have to be isolated  from the rest of the herd for two weeks  in order to prevent the possible spread  of disease  the rescuers freed the animals from all  their ropes and chains  [Music]  has provided a new home for well over  100 elephants  a home where they are no longer forced  to put on a show  where they can simply be elephants  you

